      "seq": 50,
      "player": "DSV3 Proud",
      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "Now it's my turn 2 postcombat main phase. I can play lands - I have Bloodstained Mire and Watery Grave available. I also see I drew a card: Abhorrent Oculus (2U 5/5 flying with a graveyard cost). I'm at 18 life, opponent at 20.\n\
\n\
I need to decide which land to play. I have Blood Crypt (BR) untapped. I want to cast either Emperor of Bones (1B) or Psychic Frog (UB) on my next turn.\n\
\n\
If I play Watery Grave:\n\
- I can pay 2 life to have it enter untapped\n\
- Next turn I'll have UB available for Psychic Frog, and B available for Emperor of Bones\n\
- Total life: 16 after paying\n\
\n\
If I play Bloodstained Mire:\n\
- I can fetch for Swamp or Mountain\n\
- Cost 1 life, land enters tapped\n\
- Next turn I'd have B available for Emperor of Bones, but not UB for Psychic Frog unless I fetch for Mountain and already have Watery Grave\n\
- Actually, I could fetch for Swamp, have BB available next turn (Blood Crypt + Swamp)\n\
\n\
Actually, thinking about my hand:\n\
- Emperor of Bones (1B) - can cast with just Blood Crypt\n\
- Psychic Frog (UB) - needs both U and B\n\
- Abhorrent Oculus (2U) - needs UU\n\
- Unearth (B) - can cast with any black source\n\
\n\
I should play Watery Grave to enable Psychic Frog. Psychic Frog is a better card - it's a 1/2 that draws cards on damage and has growth potential. Emperor of Bones is fine but requires setup.\n\
