- I could play Bloodstained Mire, then fetch for a basic Swamp/Mountain next turn\n\
- I could cast Psychic Frog (UB) - need to tap both lands\n\
- I could adapt Emperor of Bones (1B) - tap Watery Grave for B\n\
- I could cast Unearth (B) - but nothing good in graveyard yet\n\
\n\
Actually, looking at Emperor of Bones adapt ability: {1}{B}: Adapt 2. (If this creature has no +1/+1 counters on it, put two +1/+1 counters on it.) Then: Whenever one or more +1/+1 counters are put on {this}, put a creature card exiled with {this} onto the battlefield under your control with a finality counter on it. It gains haste. Sacrifice it at the beginning of the next end step.\n\
\n\
I have Archon of Cruelty in my graveyard! That's MV 8, too big for Unearth but could be reanimated by Emperor of Bones if I adapt it. But I need to exile a creature card from a graveyard first with Emperor's trigger at beginning of combat.\n\
\n\
Actually, Emperor of Bones has: \"At the beginning of combat on your turn, exile up to one target card from a graveyard.\" So on my combat step, I can exile Archon of Cruelty from my graveyard. Then if I adapt Emperor of Bones (putting counters on it), it will reanimate the exiled creature.\n\
\n\
That's a powerful play! I should do that.\n\
\n\
Plan:\n\
1. Play Bloodstained Mire (enters untapped)\n\
2. Go to combat, exile Archon of Cruelty from my graveyard with Emperor trigger\n\
3. After combat (or during main phase 2), adapt Emperor of Bones ({1}{B}) to put 2 +1/+1 counters on it\n\
4. Trigger: reanimate Archon of Cruelty with haste, sacrifice at end of turn\n\
\n\
But Archon of Cruelty is 6/6 flying with powerful ETB/attack trigger. Even if sacrificed at end of turn, I get the ETB trigger: target opponent sacrifices a creature/planeswalker, discards a card, loses 3 life, I draw a card and gain 3 life.\n\
\n\
That's huge value! I should do this.\n\
\n\
