      "reasoning": "Attackers declared and tapped. I have priority. Could activate abilities or cast spells.\n\
\n\
I could adapt Emperor (1B) but it already has counters, adapt won't do anything.\n\
\n\
Could discard a card to put +1/+1 counter on Psychic Frog, making it 2/3. Or give it flying by exiling three cards from my graveyard.\n\
\n\
But Psychic Frog already attacking, flying might be irrelevant unless opponent has a flying blocker (they don't). The +1/+1 counter could increase damage from 1 to 2. That's an extra damage, bringing opponent from 2 to 0 if they take 6 total instead of 5.\n\
\n\
Wait, if I give Psychic Frog +1/+1 counter, it becomes 2/3, deals 2 damage. Combined with Emperor's 4 = 6 damage. Opponent at 7 life, they'd go to 1 life.\n\
\n\
But we want to kill them this turn. If opponent has no blockers, 5 damage leaves them at 2 life. Not lethal.\n\
\n\
If I can increase Psychic Frog's power, we can get lethal. Options:\n\
1. Discard a card to put +1/+1 counter on Psychic Frog (cost: discard a card). I have Unearth, Abhorrent Oculus, Gran-Gran, etc. Could discard an Unearth.\n\
2. Exile three cards from graveyard to give flying (doesn't increase power).\n\
3. Cast Unearth to reanimate something? Could reanimate Archon of Cruelty? No, Archon is MV 8, Unearth only MV 3 or less.\n\
\n\
I have Faithless Looting in graveyard (flashback 2R) but can't cast.\n\
\n\
Better to discard a card to buff Psychic Frog. That gives +1 damage, bringing total to 6. Opponent at 7 life -> 1 life left. Still not lethal.\n\
\n\
Wait, need 7 damage. Emperor 4 + Psychic Frog 1 = 5. With +1/+1 counter, total 6. Need one more.\n\
\n\
Maybe opponent will play a creature that I can Fatal Push? Not relevant.\n\
\n\
I could adapt Emperor? Actually adapt puts two +1/+1 counters if it has no counters. Emperor already has two counters, adapt does nothing.\n\
\n\
Maybe I should hold up Fatal Push for opponent's potential creature.\n\
\n\
But we need to maximize damage. Could I cast Gran-Gran? It's a 1/2 for U, could attack but summoning sick.\n\
\n\
Alternatively, I could cast Unearth to reanimate something like Faithless Looting? Not a creature.\n\
\n\
Wait, I have Archon of Cruelty exiled by Emperor. If I put more +1/+1 counters on Emperor, its triggered ability will put Archon onto battlefield with haste! That's huge.\n\
\n\
Emperor's ability: \"Whenever one or more +1/+1 counters are put on this, put a creature card exiled with this onto the battlefield under your control with a finality counter on it. It gains haste. Sacrifice it at the beginning of the next end step.\"\n\
\n\
If I adapt Emperor (1B) when it already has counters? Adapt only works if it has no +1/+1 counters. It has counters, so adapt won't put counters.\n\
\n\
But I could remove counters? Not possible.\n\
\n\
Maybe I can play a different +1/+1 counter source? Not available.\n\
\n\
What about Psychic Frog's discard ability? That puts counter on Psychic Frog, not Emperor.\n\
\n\
So can't trigger Emperor.\n\
\n\
Thus, we attack for 5 (or 6). Opponent at 7 -> 2 (or 1). Not lethal.\n\
\n\
But opponent might have a removal spell to kill Emperor before damage. If they kill Emperor, damage reduces to 1 (Psychic Frog). That's worse.\n\
\n\
I should hold up Fatal Push to kill any creature they play, but not relevant.\n\
\n\
Maybe I should pass priority and see if opponent does anything. If they have no response, damage goes through.\n\
\n\
Let me pass priority.\n\
\n\
